    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • XPENG Reveals G9L at the 2026 Paris Motor Show, Dubbed As the Ultimate \"Large SUV for the AI Era\"\nTesla Left Intriguing Hints in the Roadster Demo Confirmation, Here's How To Watch the Livestream\n6 photos\nPhoto: Tesla\nTesla appears to keep its promise about the Roadster demonstration on October 15, confirming the livestream at 7:55 PM CST. The time is another nod to the Back to the Future movies, with Musk pointing to it with a \"Timing is everything\" tweet. Based on a NOTAM filed with the FAA, SpaceX closed the space around its Waco, TX, testing facility on Wednesday, supposedly to rehearse the demo.\nAmong all the promises Elon Musk and Tesla made, the Roadster has been the most controversial. Announced in 2017 as a \"one more thing\" during the Tesla Semi launch, the Roadster 2.0 should've started production in 2020. The pandemic certainly muddied the waters, but the Roadster soon became an afterthought, and soon after that Tesla stopped considering itself a carmaker.\nElon Musk's company has since abandoned several car projects, including an affordable compact and the successors to the Model S and Model X. However, it never quite gave up on the Roadster, insisting that it's still on the roadmap, with solid plans to produce it. That was a small consolation for those who paid a $50,000 deposit for the Roadster, not to mention those who paid the full $250,000 price for a Founder Edition model.\nEarlier this year, Tesla announced an epic Roadster demo on October 1, which was later postponed to October 15 due to adverse weather conditions. One day before the new schedule, Tesla confirmed that the Roadster demo would, indeed, take place on October 15 at 7:55 PM CST. The time is significant, something Elon Musk was quick to emphasize in a post on Twitter.\nSimilar to the \"Where we're going\" easter egg in the original teaser image, the time of the livestream is a direct reference to the Back to the Future movie. I'm not a fan of the series, but according to some, 7:55 PM, or rather 19:55, is a nod to 1955, the year Marty goes back in the movie. According to others, 7:55 is also the time shown in the opening scene of the Back to the Future movie.\nOthers believe that 7:55, together with Musk's specific use of words ( \"Timing is everything\" ), might indicate that the Roadster could complete a quarter mile in 7.55 seconds. The fastest production vehicle is currently the Rimac Nevera R, which does the quarter mile in 7.90 seconds. If the 7.55 estimate is right, it would make the Tesla Roadster the fastest production vehicle.\nRegardless of these speculations, Tesla fans fully expect the Roadster to fly or at least hover during the October 15 demo event. If Tesla delivers less than that, the electric sports car is doomed before even starting production. Which, based on conservative estimates, should not happen for at least another year, if ever.\nStill, the Roadster demo remains the most exciting Tesla event in years, and everyone is eager to watch it live. Tesla will livestream it on X starting at 7:55 PM CST on October 15. This translates to 8:55 PM EDT and 5:55 PM PDT. Europeans would be able to tune in on October 16 at 1:55 AM (UK/GMT) and 2:55 AM CEST (Central Europe). Similarly, people in Asia could watch the livestream on October 16, from 8:55 AM (China) and 9:55 AM (Japan). Timing is everything — Elon Musk (@elonmusk) October 14, 2026\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\ntesla roadster Tesla back to the future Elon Musk\nAbout the author: Cristian Agatie\nAfter his childhood dream of becoming a \"tractor operator\" didn't pan out, Cristian turned to journalism, first in print and later moving to online media. His top interests are electric vehicles and new energy solutions. Full profile\nUP NEXT He Bought a New Chevy Corvette in April 2026 and He Wants It Gone After Less Than 700 Miles",
